cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Calabi–Yau Projection Lab"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sordo Martínez"
    given-names: "Pedro"
    email: "amurlaniakea@gmail.com"
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: 2026-11-17
repository-code: "https://github.com/amurlaniakea/calabi-yau-projection-lab"
license: "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
abstract: >
  Zero-dependency educational laboratory for projecting, slicing and
  visually encoding higher-dimensional geometric objects onto 2D planes.
  Includes deterministic orthogonal projections, toy manifolds, Clifford
  torus, Fermat Calabi-Yau-like patches, exact Fermat topology, a local
  affine chart of the quintic Calabi-Yau threefold in R^8 with five
  complex fifth-root branches, reproducible SVG/JSON outputs, a static
  quintic branch gallery, an interactive web demo, and approximate
  Fubini-Study induced metric diagnostics. This repository does not
  compute Ricci-flat Calabi-Yau metrics, does not solve the complex
  Monge-Ampere equation, and does not simulate string theory physics.
keywords:
  - Calabi-Yau
  - quintic threefold
  - mathematical visualization
  - reproducible research
  - zero dependencies
  - projection
  - Clifford torus
  - Fermat topology
  - Fubini-Study metric
  - educational software
